# DMA Tapeout Project Context

This repo is a Tiny Tapeout scatter-gather DMA project in **Phase 2** (V1 feature RTL under `src/rtl/`; cocotb M0–M3 accepted; manual IHP LibreLane harden closed 1x1 @ 66 MHz), targeting **IHP SG13G2 / TTIHP26b** (D27).

## Before nontrivial work

Read `docs/llm/00-index.md` and the files it lists for the task at hand. Prefer those docs over chat memory. For local ASIC harden / LibreLane / area: `docs/llm/13-hardening-librelane.md` (human: `docs/human/architecture/hardening.md`).

When discussing PSRAM timing parameters, testbench timing parameters, or verification IDs (`Q-*`, `FP-*`, etc.), define each term inline on first use; see `.cursor/rules/verification-vocabulary.mdc`.

Human summaries live in `docs/human/` (condensed, not stubs). Every durable fact in `docs/llm/` must appear in `docs/human/` in some form; llm elaborates, it does not hold private truth. Do not grow human docs into a second full dump, and do not leave new requirements llm-only behind a pointer (anti-pattern: `CHK-*` only in `docs/llm/verification/06-checkers.md`).

## Hard constraints

- Budget: **2 Tiny Tapeout tiles max**; treat ~500 DFFs as a soft ceiling (first harden: ~158 DFFs; 1x1 fits at 66 MHz)
- PDK / shuttle: **ihp-sg13g2** / **TTIHP26b** (not sky130); do not cite sky130 GPIO MHz ratings as binding
- Start from scratch; TinyDMA-2C is prior art only, not a code source
- Obsidian notes under `C:\Users\lahnb\Documents\Obsidian Vault\Projects\Tiny Tapeout\` are **read-only**
- Prefer shipping a smaller verified V1 over late feature creep
- When proposing features, state DFF / tile impact
- **Memory scope (D11/D12/D19):** both PSRAM devices are DMA endpoints (incl. cross-device); V1 is bulk memcpy via 11-byte TCDs (`ptr[23]` device, `QUIT` end-of-chain; no ALU/ring/cond-stop); ASIC flash R/W is post-V1; see `docs/llm/10-post-v1-features.md`

